#N canvas 40 40 900 460 12;
#X text 20 20 shell -- A DO-NOTHING STAND-IN so the patch can be syntax-checked on the Mac. The real [shell] is an external that ships on the Organelle (/root/Pd/externals \, on the path via .pdsettings) and does not exist in vanilla Pd., f 58;
#X text 20 110 THIS FOLDER IS NEVER DEPLOYED. tools/deploy.sh adds it with -path for the local check only \, so on the device the real external wins. If a file named shell.pd ever reaches the patch folder it will SHADOW the external and MIDI wiring will silently stop happening., f 58;
#X obj 20 240 inlet;
#X obj 20 300 outlet;
#X text 200 240 swallowed: no command runs \, and nothing is emitted \, which is exactly what a check that only asks "does every object exist" needs., f 40;
#X text 20 360 If you find yourself wanting this to actually do something \, you want the real thing -- run the patch on the device instead \, see ref/conventions.md \, There IS a console., f 58;
